    Deploy Act 19: failure-count office reset, durable handoff queue, commit-age signal
    
    Implements enacted Act 19 (Office Continuity and Handoff Integrity Act,
    8-0-0) as bounded POSIX /bin/sh changes:
    
    - government/office-continuity.sh (new): shared supervisor helpers. Durable
      per-office failure record; reset after 3 consecutive transient failures
      within a 30-minute window regardless of observed state (1800 s cooldown);
      progress guard (durable commit between failures breaks the streak);
      permanent failures surfaced, not reset; per-office commit-age signal
      emitted while the office has uncommitted work.
    - government/handoff-queue.sh (new): atomic durable records/handoffs/ queue
      (add/list-open/mark); the steer IS the queue entry at steer time.
    - branch-bootstrap.sh, clerk-liveness.sh: state-triggered endpoint-only
      reset replaced by the failure-count reset; transient class covers
      unrecognized_backend_failure and runtime transient=true.
    - executive-cycle.sh: reads the handoff queue FIRST; no generic
      eligible-issue dispatch while an open handoff exists; no dispatch at all
      on script failure before the queue read.
    - Tests: new act19-office-continuity-smoke.sh (P1/P1a/P2/P3 mechanisms);
      clerk-liveness-smoke and executive-recovery-timing-smoke updated to the
      failure-count semantics; executive-cycle-smoke fixture ships the queue
      tool; boot-smoke seeds the janitor timers (host-independent).
    - records/DEPLOYMENT-2026-10-19-act19-office-continuity.md: before/after
      deployment evidence; RECOVERY-RUNBOOK.md notes the Act 19 mechanisms.
    
    No Constitution/boot/voting/seat/quorum change; no new agent, model or
    worker cap. Full suite: dash tests/run-all.sh -> All Viche tests passed.

